    "title": "Duke basketball vs UConn game time set for March Madness Elite 8",
    "text": "March 28, 2026, 12:21 a.m. ETDuke basketball will tip off against No. 2 seed UConn at 5:05 p.m. ET on Sunday, March 29, in the 2026 Men's NCAA Tournament Elite 8.The No. 1 seeded Blue Devils (35-2) and head coach Jon Scheyer will face the No. 2 seeded Huskies and head coach Dan Hurley at Capital One Arena in Washington, D.C on CBS.Duke is coming off a 70-65 win over 5-seeded St. John's in the Elite 8 behind a huge return from Caleb Foster. The junior guard scored 11 points, all in the second half, of his long awaited return. UConn defeated No. 3 Michigan State, 67-63, to earn a spot in the Elite 8.Sunday night's winner advances to the Final Four in Indianapolis, Indiana. Duke is looking to win its sixth national championship.Here's game time and how to watch Duke vs. UConn:Watch Duke basketball in March MadnessWhat time does Duke play UConn in 2026 NCAA tournament Elite 8?Date: Sunday, March 29Time: 5:05 p.m. ETDuke plays UConn at 5:05 p.m. ET in the 2026 NCAA Tournament on Sunday, March 29, at Capital One Arena in Washington, D.C.What channel is Duke vs UConn in March Madness Elite 8?TV Channel: CBSStream: FuboThe Duke vs. UConn game will air on CBS and can be streamed on Fubo, which offers a free trial to new subscribers.Duke basketball schedule 2025-26Below are the past five games of Duke's 2025-26 basketball season. For the full schedule, click here.March 21, 2026: Duke 81, TCU 58 (NCAA Tournament round two)March 12, 2026: Duke 80, Florida State 79 (ACC Tournament quarterfinals)March 13, 2026: Duke 73, Clemson 61 (ACC Tournament semifinals)March 14, 2026: Duke 74, Virginia 70 (ACC Tournament championship game)March 19, 2026: Dule 71, Siena 65 (NCAA Tournament round one)UConn basketball schedule 2025-26Below are the past five games of UConn's 2025-26 basketball season. For the full schedule, click here.March 13, 2026: UConn 67, Georgetown 51 (Big East semifinals)March 14, 2026: St. John's 72, UConn 52 (Big East championship game)March 20, 2026: UConn 82, Furman 71 (NCAA Tournament round one)March 22, 2026: UConn 73, UCLA 57 (NCAA Tournament round two)March 27, 2026: UConn 67, Michigan State 63Anna Snyder covers Duke for The Fayetteville Observer as part of the USA TODAY Network. Reach her at asnyder@usatodayco.com or follow her @annaesnydr on X, formerly known as Twitter.",
